{"name":"Canopy","hex":"#728f02","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"canopy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A high cover providing shelter, such as a cloth supported above an object, particularly over a bed.","Any overhanging or projecting roof structure, typically over entrances or doors."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with or as if with a canopy.","To go through the canopy of a forest on a zipline."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/canopy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Canopy (botany)","blocks":[{"text":"In biology, the canopy is the aboveground portion of a plant cropping or crop, formed by the collection of individual plant crowns. In forest ecology, the canopy is the upper layer or habitat zone, formed by mature tree crowns and including other biological organisms. The communities that inhabit the canopy layer are thought to be involved in maintaining forest diversity, resilience, and functioning. Shade trees normally have a dense canopy that blocks light from lower growing plants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/JigsawCanopy.jpg/330px-JigsawCanopy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canopy_(botany)","wikidata":"Q1134228"},{"title":"Canopy (grape)","blocks":[{"text":"In viticulture, the canopy of a grapevine includes the parts of the vine visible aboveground - the trunk, cordon, stems, leaves, flowers, and fruit. The canopy plays a key role in light energy capture via photosynthesis, water use as regulated by transpiration, and microclimate of ripening grapes. Canopy management is an important aspect of viticulture due to its effect on grape yields, quality, vigor, and the prevention of grape diseases. Various viticulture problems, such as uneven grape ripening, sunburn, and frost damage, can be addressed by skillful canopy management. In addition to pruning and leaf trim, the canopy is often trained on trellis systems to guide its growth and assist in access for ongoing management and harvest."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Grape_vines.jpg/330px-Grape_vines.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canopy_(grape)","wikidata":"Q5033434"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Havelock_Island%2C_Canopy_of_tropical_moist_evergreen_forest%2C_Andaman_Islands.jpg/500px-Havelock_Island%2C_Canopy_of_tropical_moist_evergreen_forest%2C_Andaman_Islands.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Havelock_Island%2C_Canopy_of_tropical_moist_evergreen_forest%2C_Andaman_Islands.jpg/1280px-Havelock_Island%2C_Canopy_of_tropical_moist_evergreen_forest%2C_Andaman_Islands.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Havelock_Island%2C_Canopy_of_tropical_moist_evergreen_forest%2C_Andaman_Islands.jpg/500px-Havelock_Island%2C_Canopy_of_tropical_moist_evergreen_forest%2C_Andaman_Islands.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Canopy of tropical evergreen forest, Andaman Islands","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHavelock_Island%2C_Canopy_of_tropical_moist_evergreen_forest%2C_Andaman_Islands.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Khao_Sok_primary_tropical_rainforest%2C_southern_Thailand.jpg/500px-Khao_Sok_primary_tropical_rainforest%2C_southern_Thailand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Khao_Sok_primary_tropical_rainforest%2C_southern_Thailand.jpg/1280px-Khao_Sok_primary_tropical_rainforest%2C_southern_Thailand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_c